HADOW_PREVIEW is the sole live runtime branch flag controlling the preview router. ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is a harmless alias that normalizes to the same path. PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY is parsed but only affects reporting labels, not runtime behavior.\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"cleanup_plan\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"keep\\\",\n      \\\"blockers\\\": [],\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"This is the primary live flag controlling the preview router. It must remain active and functional.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"deprecate\\\",\n      \\\"blockers\\\": [\\\"legacy deploy manifests may still reference it\\\"],\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Alias with no independent runtime branch. Can be deprecated once legacy deploy manifests are migrated to use ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW directly.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"flag\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"telemetry_first\\\",\n      \\\"blockers\\\": [\\\"operator notes and reporting pipelines may depend on the force_legacy_seen signal\\\"],\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Parser hit exists but no runtime branch. Before removal, verify that reporting pipelines and operator tooling no longer depend on the force_legacy_seen flag in the plan output.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"assumption_ledger\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"observed\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW runtime branch\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"Confirmed in runtime.py conditional check on shadow_enabled\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"observed\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 alias normalization\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"Confirmed in config.py elif branch mapping to shadow path\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"missing\\\",\n      \\\"topic\\\": \\\"PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY downstream consumers\\\",\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"No evidence of runtime branching; legacy